{
 "id": "L4",
 "n": 4,
 "title": "Around town, shopping, time",
 "goal": "Ask where things are, get a taxi, shop and pay in won, and tell the time and day.",
 "notes": [
  {
   "h": "Where is it? Here, there, over there",
   "p": "{{어디예요?}} asks where something is. Answer with {{여기}} (here, near me), {{거기}} (there, near you) or {{저기}} (over there, away from both of us), plus {{예요}}. Directions are polite commands ending in {{-세요}}: {{쭉 가세요}} (go straight).",
   "ex": [
    [
     "화장실이 어디예요?",
     "Where's the restroom?"
    ],
    [
     "저기예요",
     "It's over there."
    ],
    [
     "오른쪽으로 가세요",
     "Go to the right."
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "h": "To, at and by",
   "p": "{{에}} marks where you are going and when something happens: {{한국에 가요}}, {{월요일에}}, {{세 시에}}. Never add {{에}} to {{오늘}}, {{내일}}, {{어제}} or {{지금}}. {{으로}} / {{로}} means \"toward\" or \"by (a way of travel)\": {{공항으로}}, {{지하철로}}, {{택시로}}. Use {{로}} after a vowel or after ㄹ, and {{으로}} after any other consonant. {{에서}} means \"from\" a place: {{여기에서}}.",
   "ex": [
    [
     "내일 한국에 가요",
     "I'm going to Korea tomorrow."
    ],
    [
     "공항으로 가 주세요",
     "To the airport, please."
    ],
    [
     "지하철로 가요",
     "I'm going by subway."
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "h": "Money",
   "p": "Prices use Sino-Korean numbers plus {{원}}. Korean groups big numbers in ten-thousands ({{만}}), not thousands: 10,000 is {{만}}, 50,000 is {{오만}}, 15,000 is {{만 오천}}. For 100, 1,000 and 10,000 just say {{백}}, {{천}}, {{만}} with no \"one\" in front. Ask the price with {{얼마예요?}}",
   "ex": [
    [
     "이거 얼마예요?",
     "How much is this?"
    ],
    [
     "오천 원이에요",
     "It's 5,000 won."
    ],
    [
     "만 오천 원이에요",
     "It's 15,000 won."
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "h": "Telling time and days",
   "p": "Hours use native numbers (shortened before {{시}}: {{한 시}}, {{두 시}}, {{세 시}}, {{네 시}}), and minutes use Sino-Korean: {{세 시 삼십 분}} is 3:30. {{반}} means half past: {{세 시 반}}. Eleven and twelve o'clock are {{열한 시}} and {{열두 시}}. The days of the week all end in {{요일}}, from {{월요일}} (Monday) to {{일요일}} (Sunday).",
   "ex": [
    [
     "지금 몇 시예요?",
     "What time is it now?"
    ],
    [
     "두 시 십 분이에요",
     "It's 2:10."
    ],
    [
     "토요일에 가요",
     "I'm going on Saturday."
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "h": "Wanting, and sounds to watch",
   "p": "Add {{-고 싶어요}} to a verb stem to say you want to do it: {{가다}} becomes {{가고 싶어요}}, {{사다}} becomes {{사고 싶어요}}. Listen for the tense ㅆ: {{싸요}} (it's cheap) and {{사요}} (I buy) differ only in that sound. A final consonant links into the next vowel: {{월요일}} is said {{워료일}} and {{목요일}} is said {{모교일}}. After a final t or p sound, the next consonant tenses: {{몇 시}} sounds like {{멷 씨}} and {{십 분}} like {{십 뿐}}.",
   "ex": [
    [
     "이거 사고 싶어요",
     "I'd like to buy this."
    ],
    [
     "이거 싸요",
     "This is cheap."
    ],
    [
     "목요일에 가고 싶어요",
     "I want to go on Thursday."
    ]
   ]
  }
 ],
